Package: kissbufd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: ax25-tools
Description: Transmit buffer manager for KISS TNCs with ACKmode flow control
 kissbufd sits between a host KISS program such as kissattach and a TNC
 that supports the KISS ACKMODE extension but has no hardware flow
 control, such as the NinoTNC. It exposes a pseudo-terminal to the host.
 .
 Frames are released to the TNC only while the raw KISS bytes on the TNC
 stay under a configurable share of its buffer; ACKMODE acknowledgements
 provide the backpressure. Host ACKMODE frames are passed through via an
 ID translation table, plain KISS frames are tracked internally.
 .
 A systemd template unit runs one instance per configuration file in
 /etc/kissbufd/.
